From c7bbb139cc9d28a1be56e897ece666f8e8aa5329 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:54:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Heat transfer and geometry: review (sign of the transient
 term, NURBS)

- The test behaviour HeatStorage returned the rate of the enthalpy,
  r = C dT/dt, as the documentation of TransientHeatTransfer says. With the
  stationary heat transfer behaviour integrators of mfem-mgis, whose
  residual is the integral of grad(N) . j with j = -k grad(T), this solves
  the backward heat equation: the comparisons of HeatTransferKernelsTest
  compared computations of this wrong model. HeatStorage now returns
  r = -C dT/dt, and the documentation of TransientHeatTransfer states the
  sign convention and that the gradients of the state at the beginning of
  the first time step must be initialised with the initial temperature.
  HeatTransferKernelsTest checks that the transient temperature lags
  behind the stationary one (by 16 to 37 K on average), a check that does
  not depend on the computation path.
- HeatTransferKernelsTest and MicromorphicKernelsTest check the diagonal of
  the tangent operator applied without assembly against the assembled one,
  after the resolution of the last time step and before the update of the
  materials (a doubled diagonal was not detected).
- computeElementsGeometry refuses the NURBS meshes, whose element
  transformations are not given by the degrees of freedom of the nodes
  (jacobians wrong by up to 96%), and checks that the cached values of the
  shape functions belong to the finite element of the unknowns.
  ElementsGeometryTest checks the refusal of a NURBS mesh and that the
  jacobians are kept when the nodes of the mesh are modified.
- Documentation: the traits of the behaviour integrators commit them to
  the standard computations reproduced by the kernels (or to override
  supportsKernels); the version of the stiffness matrices kernel used
  without device; the recognition of the behaviours by their structure;
  the descriptions of the files and of the tests.
- The variants of BatchIntegrationTest, HeatTransferKernelsTest and
  MicromorphicKernelsTest on the debug device of MFEM are only registered
  in the optimised builds (they take one or two minutes in Release).

Mutations detected: sign of the transient term (lag), doubled diagonal,
acceptance of NURBS meshes.
